[CHANGE] benchmark_3/parts/semver_solver_multi/pretense/dependency_solver_pretense.py: Rewrite resolve to model the backtracking_solver_ext reference mechanics exactly: build accumulated constraints as (requester, range) entries, select the unassigned package with the fewest viable candidates (lexical tie-break), assign the highest descending-precedence candidate, merge its dependencies into a snapshot-safe mapping (no mutation during iteration, eliminating the RuntimeError), and record ordered derivation steps in the reference's 'Assign <pkg> to <version>' format so selected_versions and derivation_steps match the required ResolutionOutcome. Added a shared descending-precedence release ordering helper used by both get_releases and resolve.
