[BLAME] benchmark_3/parts/semver_solver_multi/pretense/dependency_solver_impl_pretense.py: The deterministic scenario suite covers only successful repository registration/query and successful resolution, so it never exercises the contracted negative paths declared in low/dependency_solver.pyi. Missing required scenarios: (1) looking up an unregistered package name MUST raise PackageNotFoundError per the get_releases precondition; (2) resolve MUST raise ResolutionConflictError when a root or transitive dependency references a package absent from the repository, and when accumulated constraints are mutually unsatisfiable, reporting the conflicting packages and a derivation explanation; (3) resolve MUST backtrack past an unviable higher-precedence candidate, both to a later viable release (verifying highest-precedence-compatible selection) and to exhaustive failure; and (4) resolve MUST detect and report a conflict where a selected release's dependency constraint contradicts an already-assigned package. The library change that pruned the empty-conflict-trail fallback added none of these scenario transitions, so the given contract-required failure and backtracking paths remain unexercised and full statement coverage cannot be certified. Add fixed scenario tests that drive each of these contracted transitions.
[BLAME] benchmark_3/parts/semver_solver_multi/pretense/semver_core_impl_pretense.py: The deterministic scenario suite here exercises only valid parses and precedence comparisons that differ in major/minor/patch or in prerelease sequences with a numeric-versus-textual or length difference, so several contracted behaviors in low/semver_core.pyi are never exercised. Missing required cases: (1) the parse_version precondition that malformed or leading-zero version strings MUST raise InvalidVersionError; (2) the postcondition that two prerelease identifiers which are both numeric MUST be compared as integers, covering both equal and unequal values; (3) the postcondition that two prerelease identifiers which are both textual MUST be compared ASCII-lexicographically; and (4) the postcondition that two versions with identical major, minor, patch and identical non-empty prerelease sequences MUST compare equal (zero), with build metadata ignored. The scenario additions described in the change did not cover these contracted parse-failure and prerelease-comparison cases, so full statement coverage cannot be certified. Extend the fixed scenario tests to drive each of these contracted branches.
[BLAME] benchmark_3/parts/semver_solver_multi/pretense/semver_range_impl_pretense.py: The deterministic scenario suite covers only positive-path ranges (trimming, basic comparators, non-zero-major caret/tilde, minor wildcards, hyphen and union parsing, prerelease gating), so the checked preconditions and expansion rules contracted in low/semver_range.pyi remain unexercised: the parse_range precondition that empty or whitespace-only expressions, comma delimiters, empty union clauses, bare partial versions lacking wildcard characters (such as 1, 1.2, ^0.0, 1.2 - 2.3), and other malformed syntax MUST raise InvalidRangeError; the wildcard forms M.x and M.* including their inclusive lower and exclusive upper boundaries; every relational comparator, including != and >, combined with a wildcard target, including targets truncated to a vacuous or unsatisfiable expansion; caret prefixes anchored on zero-major versions (first non-zero minor and all-zero cases) and caret/tilde prefixes applied to wildcard targets; and hyphen ranges whose lower or upper endpoint is a wildcard. The latest change only annotated the structurally unreachable malformed-clause guard, which resolves that single span; the contracted invalid-input and wildcard/zero-major expansions above are reachable under the specification and remain uncovered, so full statement coverage cannot be certified without fixed scenario coverage of these cases.
[CHANGE] benchmark_3/parts/semver_solver_multi/pretense/dependency_solver_impl_pretense.py: Add the contracted negative and backtracking scenarios while mirroring the reference solver in the model: (1) get_releases on an unregistered package raises PackageNotFoundError; (2) resolve raises ResolutionConflictError for absent root packages, absent transitive packages, and mutually unsatisfiable accumulated constraints, asserting conflicting_packages and a non-empty explanation; (3) a genuine backtracking scenario where the highest-precedence alpha is rejected by beta's dependency and the solver backtracks to a lower viable alpha, as well as exhaustive-failure backtracking; (4) a conflict where a selected release's dependency contradicts an already-assigned package. The interface model resolve now runs the full reference MRV depth-first search with backtracking and conflict-trail collection so successful backtracking outcomes and ordered derivation steps match the concrete solver.
[CHANGE] benchmark_3/parts/semver_solver_multi/pretense/semver_core_impl_pretense.py: Extend the fixed scenario suite to cover the contracted branches: parse_version now asserts InvalidVersionError for leading-zero numerics, truncated components, non-numeric text, and extra components; compare_precedence now covers numeric prerelease identifiers compared as integers (unequal 10 vs 9 and equal 2 vs 2), textual identifiers compared ASCII-lexicographically, and identical non-empty prerelease sequences with differing build metadata comparing equal. The interface parse_version model now validates SemVer 2.0.0 grammar and raises InvalidVersionError for the same malformed inputs, so model and concrete engine agree on parse-failure behavior.
[CHANGE] benchmark_3/parts/semver_solver_multi/pretense/semver_range_impl_pretense.py: Extend the fixed scenario suite to cover the contracted preconditions and expansion rules: parse_range now asserts InvalidRangeError for empty/whitespace expressions, comma delimiters, empty union clauses, bare partial versions without wildcards (1, 1.2, ^0.0, 1.2 - 2.3), and malformed syntax; added M.x/M.* inclusive-lower/exclusive-upper boundary scenarios; relational comparators (>=, >, <=, <, !=) with wildcard targets including vacuous/unsatisfiable * expansions; caret ranges anchored on zero-major versions (^0.2.3, ^0.0.3); caret/tilde prefixes over wildcard targets; and hyphen ranges with wildcard endpoints. The interface model now validates range syntax and raises InvalidRangeError consistently, and normalizes wildcard targets per operator (including caret/tilde and hyphen endpoints) so model and engine agree.
